verses.text:
Listen, you peoples, all of you;
pay attention, earth, and all that fills it;
and let the Lord Yahweh be witness against you,
the Lord from his holy temple.

All her carved idols will be smashed to bits,
all her earnings{e} burned with fire,
and all her images I will make a desolation;
for from a prostitute’s fee she gathered them,
and to a prostitute’s fee they will return.”

For this I will lament and wail;
I will go barefoot and naked;
I will make lament like the jackals
and mourning like the ostriches.

For her wound cannot be healed;
it has come even to Judah;
it has reached the gate of my people,
even to Jerusalem.

Tell it not in Gath;{f}
weep not at all.
In Beth-leaphrah{g}
roll yourself in the dust.

Pass on your way,
inhabitants of Shaphir,{h} in shameful nakedness;
the inhabitants of Zaanan{i} do not come out;
Beth-ezel is wailing,
it will take away from you its support.{j}

So you will give parting gifts{m}
to Moresheth-gath;
the houses of Achzib{n} will be a deception
to Israel’s kings.

Again I will bring a conqueror{o} upon you,
inhabitants of Mareshah;
the glory of Israel
will come to Adullam.{p}

“Stop your preaching,” so they preach.{b}
“No one should preach about these things;
shame will never catch up with us.”

“I will surely assemble all of you, Jacob;
I will surely gather the remnant of Israel;
I will bring them together like a flock in its pen,{c}
like a herd within its pasture;
it will hum with people.

you who hate good and love evil,
who tear the skin off my people{a}
and the flesh from their bones,

So night will fall on you, and no vision come;
dark will it be for you, and no divining;
the sun will set upon the prophets,
and the daylight turn black above them.

Shamed will be the seers
and abashed the diviners;
all of them will cover their lips,{b}
for God gives no answer.

He shall judge between many peoples
and settle disputes for strong nations far away;
they shall hammer their swords into plow blades
and their spears into pruning knives;
nation shall not raise sword against nation,
nor shall they train for war any longer.

Writhe and groan,{f} Daughter Zion,
like a woman giving birth;
for now you must go out from the town
and lodge in the countryside;
you will go to Babylon.
There you will be rescued;
there Yahweh will redeem you
from the grip of your enemies.

Rise up and thresh, Daughter Zion,
for I will make your horn iron
and your hoofs bronze;
you will crush many peoples,
and devote their gain to Yahweh,{g}
their wealth to the Lord of all the earth.

Now muster your troops, daughter of troops;{a}
a siege is laid against us;
with a rod they strike on the cheek
the judge of Israel.

But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah,{b}
too little to be among the clans of Judah,
from you there shall come forth for me
one who is to be ruler in Israel,
whose origins are from of old,
from ancient days.{c}

And he shall be our peace.{d}
When Assyria invades our land
and marches over our citadels,
we will set up seven shepherds against it,
yes, eight princes of the people.{e}

“In that day,” declares Yahweh,
“I will cut off your horses from among you
and destroy your chariots;

Hear, you mountains, Yahweh’s lawsuit,{a}
you enduring foundations of the earth;
for Yahweh has a case against his people,
and with Israel he will argue it.

My people, recall now
what Balak, Moab’s king, schemed,
what reply Balaam son of Beor gave him,{b}
and all that took place between Shittim and Gilgal,{c}
that you may know the righteous acts{d} of Yahweh.”

He has told you, O mortal,{e} what is good;
and what does Yahweh ask of you
but to do justice, to love faithful kindness,{f}
and to walk humbly{g} with your God?

The voice of Yahweh calls to the city—
and it is wisdom to fear your name:{h}
“Listen, tribe, and who appointed it!{i}

Her rich are full of violence;
her inhabitants speak lies,
and their tongue is deceit in their mouths.

You will sow but not reap;
you will tread olives but not anoint yourself with oil,
and grapes, but not drink the wine.

For you have kept the statutes of Omri{n}
and all the practices of Ahab’s house,
and you have walked in their counsels;
so I will turn you into a wasteland
and your{o} people into something to hiss at;
you will bear the scorn of my people.”

The faithful have perished from the land,
and there is no one upright among humankind;
all of them lie in ambush for blood;
each hunts his brother with a net.

Do not rely on a companion;
do not lean on a close friend;
even from her who lies in your arms
keep watch over the door of your lips.

For the son treats his father with contempt,
the daughter rises against her mother,
the daughter-in-law against her mother-in-law;
a man’s enemies are those of his own house.{b}

But as for me, I will watch for Yahweh;
I will wait for the God of my salvation;
my God will hear me.

On that day they will come to you
from Assyria and the cities of Egypt,{d}
and from Egypt to the River,{e}
from sea to sea and from mountain to mountain.

The nations will see and be ashamed
of all their might;
they will lay their hands on their mouths;
their ears will be deaf.

They will lick dust like a snake,
like crawling things of the earth;
they will come trembling out of their strongholds;
to Yahweh our God they will turn in dread,
and they will be afraid of you.
